{{Quote|The Senate has put a bounty on your horned little head.|[[Asajj Ventress]], to [[Ahsoka Tano]]|<ref name="Catch">{{TCW|To Catch a Jedi}}</ref>}}
'''Montrals''' were sensory organs that sprouted from the heads of both [[Togruta]] and [[Kessurian]]s. On Togruta, montrals were cone-like horns, while on Kessurians they were spines jutting from the sides of their heads.

==On Togruta==
On [[Togruta]], montrals were two hollow, cone-like horns that sprouted from the top of their skulls, forming the top of their three [[lekku]] growing below. The Togruta's montrals formed an extrasensory organ capable of sensing the movement of physical objects around them<ref name="Epic Battles">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Visual Guide: Epic Battles]]''</ref> within a scope of up to 25 [[meter]]s (82 [[Foot|feet]]).<ref name="AbEverything">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> The montrals of a Togruta grew taller with age: in adolescence, they looked like mere bumps on the head, but they jutted high above the head by adulthood.<ref name="AotG">''[[Star Wars: Aliens of the Galaxy]]''</ref> [[Gender|Male]] Togruta possessed larger and more angular montrals than females.<ref name="Kidnapped">{{TCW|Kidnapped}}</ref> The 

On the [[planet]] of [[Kiros]], the buildings of the Togruta [[artisan colony]] were shaped like montrals.<ref name="Kidnapped" /> Describing them as "horns," the [[Duros]] [[Cad Bane]] did not know the head-tails of Togruta were called montrals.<ref name="Bane's story">{{StoryCite|story=Bane's Story|book=The Clone Wars: Stories of Light and Dark}}</ref>

==On Kessurians==
On [[Kessurian]]s, montrals were located above their elongated [[ear]]s and served to increase their senses. This ability made them adept in space-perception.<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

